gui.tntsallin1client.tour.welcome.title=Welcome to the game!
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.welcome.text=Now we'll show you the client's menus in the game. Click “Next” or press Enter.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_mods.title=Client Mods
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_mods.text=“Client Mods” opens the menu with all of the client's features - displays, zoom, crosshair and much more. Let's take a look.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_mods_again.title=Client Mods in the other design
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_mods_again.text=Here too, “Client Mods” opens the menu with all features - just in this design.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.list_features.title=The features
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.list_features.text=Every row is a feature: switch it on or off on the left, fine-tune it with “Options”. The features are sorted into sections - scroll for more. Here we only look, you'll try it out in the game in a moment.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.list_search.title=Search
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.list_search.text=The search finds any feature quickly. “Done” takes you back.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.cards_card.title=The features
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.cards_card.text=In the client design every feature is a card: symbol and name on top, “Options” in the middle to fine-tune it, “Enabled”/“Disabled” at the bottom to switch it. Here we only look, you'll try it out in the game in a moment.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.cards_top.title=Search and displays
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.cards_top.text=At the top you'll find “Done”, the search and “Move/Resize” - that's where you arrange displays like the FPS counter on the screen. “Reset All” below it puts every setting back to its default.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_options.title=Key bindings
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_options.text=Many features have keys of their own, e.g. zoom or freecam. You bind them in the feature's options - or all of them together here under “Options...” → “Controls...” in the section “TNT's All-In-1 Client”.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_friends.title=Friends
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_friends.text=“Friends” in the top left shows which of your friends are online and lets you accept invites that fit this Minecraft version. The button is in the pause menu too.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_switch_to_client.title=Client Design
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_switch_to_client.text=“Client Design” switches to the client's own design - in your launcher colors. Click “Next” and we'll take a look.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_switch_to_minecraft.title=Minecraft Design
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_switch_to_minecraft.text=The logo is the design switch: clicking it switches to the regular Minecraft design. Click “Next” and we'll take a look.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_switch_back_client.title=Switching back
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_switch_back_client.text=The logo takes you back to the Minecraft design anytime. We'll ask you at the end of the tour which design you want to keep.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_switch_back_minecraft.title=Switching back
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.title_switch_back_minecraft.text=“Client Design” takes you back to the client design anytime. We'll ask you at the end of the tour which design you want to keep.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.create_world.title=Create a world
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.create_world.text=Click “Singleplayer” and then “Create New World”. Don't worry: you can delete the world again anytime later.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.open_pause.title=Open the pause menu
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.open_pause.text=Press Esc to open the pause menu.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_intro_minecraft.title=In the pause menu too
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_intro_minecraft.text=Even in the middle of the game, “Client Mods” and the “Client Design” switch are always right here in the pause menu.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_intro_client.title=In the pause menu too
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_intro_client.text=Even in the middle of the game, “Client Mods” is always right here in the pause menu - and the logo on top is the design switch again.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_switch_minecraft.title=Switch the design
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_switch_minecraft.text=Try it: click “Client Design”.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_switch_client.title=Switch the design
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_switch_client.text=Try it: click the logo.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_mods.title=Open Client Mods
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_mods.text=Now click “Client Mods”.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.menu_try.title=Switch a feature on
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.menu_try.text=Try it: switch on the FPS counter. Once you're back in the game, you'll see it in the top right corner. Then click “Next”.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.menu_options.title=Open the options
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.menu_options.text=Click “Options” next to the FPS counter.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.options_keys.title=Options and keys
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.options_keys.text=Here you fine-tune a feature, for the FPS counter e.g. its color. Features with a key of their own are bound in their options too - or all of them together in Minecraft's “Options...” → “Controls...”.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.menu_hud.title=Move displays
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.menu_hud.text=This is where you arrange displays like the FPS counter on the screen and change their size.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.menu_done.title=Back to the pause menu
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.menu_done.text=Click “Done”.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_friends.title=Friends
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.pause_friends.text=Click “Friends”.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.friends.title=Friends in the game
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.friends.text=Here you see which of your friends are online and accept invites. Inviting friends into your own world is not possible in this Minecraft version.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.finish.title=Done!
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.finish.text=That was the tour. Which design would you like to keep? You can switch anytime - on the title screen, in the pause menu or in the launcher settings.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.finish.world_hint=You can delete the tour's world anytime in the singleplayer menu.
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.finish.keep_minecraft=Minecraft Design
gui.tntsallin1client.tour.finish.keep_client=Client Design
